    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d81">

                <pb facs="0162" n="94" xml:id="pg94"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1990.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-05-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 27, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> With reference to my communications of the
                    15th instant, No. 1981, and 17th instant. No. 1984, concerning the case of
                    William Jackson, otherwise called John McCafferty, reported as under sentence of
                    death for alleged high treason in Ireland, I enclose for your information a copy
                    of a letter of the 18th instant, received at this department on the 25th, from
                    James J. Rogers, esq., of New York city.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d81-a1.xml" xpointer="d81-a1"/>
            </div>
